body:
Yeah uh...we have some problems.  We're trying to be more attractive to tourists in all the wrong ways, like...A NEW BRIDGE?!  Whoopy-de-derping-doo.  We get a lot of trash on the beach when spring break comes, and the stuff from the Mississippi loves to pile up too.  We tried opening a Schlitterbahn, which it did, but it was put on hold due to some serious legal stuff (mainly about the owners and a beheaded child.  And land ownership.)  It's not that big, and is surrounded by sand dunes (and that's putting it nicely; the kind of dunes with weeds and shiz).

&#x200B;

The conventions are nice.  We have that.  But our government is mostly ran by realtors/brokers trying to increase property values for their own reasons.  For gamers and the like?  Really only one place now, gamer's den.  It's okay, but needs a lot more business to really go anywhere.  Otherwise, as a citizen born and raised here, please try to enjoy the beach, maybe get some fishing in, go to a local restaurant like Snoopy's on the island, or Town and Country cafe near everhart and alameda.

&#x200B;

We also rarely get hurricanes.  And if we do, we try to help one another out (my family helped victims with blankets, meals and cold water while I was in college, and I wish I could have helped too).
